{"id": "EUVD-2026-102966", "enisaUuid": "f7ca3ddd-6495-3280-bf18-99f7be3e0c34", "description": "Course-tencent-cloud through 2.0.1 contains an improper restriction of authentication attempts vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to brute force 6-digit SMS/email verification codes, which are never invalidated or attempt-limited. Attackers who know a victim's phone or email can trigger a code and rotate source IPs against the password reset and verify login endpoints to take over accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T13:27:20", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/ctc-verify-code-brute-force-account-takeover", "https://github.com/xiaochong0302/course-tencent-cloud/blob/v2.0.1/app/Services/Verify.php#L27-L73", "https://github.com/xiaochong0302/course-tencent-cloud/blob/v2.0.1/app/Services/Logic/Account/PasswordReset.php", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/course-tencent-cloud-through-2.0.1-verification-code-brute-force-account-takeover"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h2mg-h5vq-xqx3", "CVE-2026-111675"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "afb2e00f-715d-3c15-904b-072d0f00806e", "product": {"name": "course-tencent-cloud", "vendor": {"name": "xiaochong0302"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4181380-9f16-3eb4-8593-bee4c4852fea", "vendor": {"name": "xiaochong0302"}}], "isExploited": false}